
[size=6][b]SaveFileManagerMod[/b][/size]

Adds buttons to name and archive save files.


[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]


[size=4][b]Naming save files[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The mod adds a "Rename" button below each save file to give them a custom name, making it easier to keep track of your saves.[/*]
[*]Names are synchronized to your Steam Cloud.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Archiving save files[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The mod adds an "Archive" button below each save file, allowing you to:[/*]
[list]
[*]Move a save to the archive, freeing up one of your precious 4 slots.[/*]
[*]Loading an archived save back into an empty slot.[/*]
[*]Swapping an active save with one from the archive.[/*]
[/list]
[*]Archived saves are still synchronized to your Steam Cloud.[/*]
[*]If you have [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/hollowknightsilksong/mods/499]More Saves[/url] installed, the archive will be the later pages of saves. In that case,[/*]
this mod will simply allow you to move saves between pages.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Dependencies[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/hollowknightsilksong/mods/26]BepInEx[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/hollow-knight-silksong/p/silksong_modding/DataManager/]DataManager[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/hollow-knight-silksong/p/silksong_modding/ModMenu/]ModMenu[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://thunderstore.io/c/hollow-knight-silksong/p/silksong_modding/I18N/]I18N[/url] (optional)[/*]
[list]
[*]The mod will be displayed in english by default. If I18N is installed, additional languages will be available.[/*]
[*]Note that currently, only english and german were checked by a human. The remaining languages are MTL/AI.[/*]
[/list]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]


[size=4][b]Managed installation[/b][/size]

This mod should be compatible with the mod management tool of your choice. If any of them don't work, please open [url=https://github.com/mich101mich/Silksong.SaveFileManagerMod/issues]an issue on GitHub[/url].


[size=4][b]Manual installation[/b][/size]

Drop the downloaded and extracted files into your game folder's [font=Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, monospace]Bepinex/plugins[/font] folder.

In order for I18N translations to work, make sure that the [font=Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, monospace]languages[/font] folder is directly adjacent to the [font=Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, monospace]SaveFileManagerMod.dll[/font] file and that both are within a subfolder (so for example [font=Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, monospace]Bepinex/plugins/SaveFileManagerMod[/font]) of plugins. Translations won't work if the files are directly inside of the plugins folder.

